  "live_records": {
    "q-82209": {
      "dom_id": "step-q82209",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Change the order of integration in the double integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14154008/assets/48a1ef0d61b8b81e2fa0649b95a329099d48a802a5339d730f2da9cf8b59f547.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It is a type II region, and its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,1\\le x\\le 2-{y}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the top boundary of the region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$$\nx=2-{y}^{2}\\,⟹\\,y=\\sqrt{2-x},\n$$\n\nand the bottom boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=0.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type I region. The type I representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{2-x}\\},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14154008/assets/22d41ecc443e1520035f52fefe524d88062432ab1643aa19b2e0b76185b191a0.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2-x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
