    "q-82196": {
      "dom_id": "step-q82196",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Change the order of integration in the double integral ${\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{2y-2}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14154008/assets/062d32beb0cab13297c21b2eab703fd5e598191c96daa93a9c27337af95a1930.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It is a type II region, and its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 2,\\,2y-2\\le x\\le 2\\}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the top boundary of the region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$$\nx=2y-2\\,⟹\\,y=\\frac{x+2}{2},\n$$\n\nand the bottom boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=1.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type I region. The type I representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le \\frac{x+2}{2}\\},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14154008/assets/543ffc57d0d32ae9a4bdefa87bd56deb7380061004b7737cf821117b4fb20e2f.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{2y-2}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{(x+2)/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-82196-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{\\int }_{(x+2)/2}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x",
              "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"18\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mstyle><mjx-texatom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-msubsup><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-lop\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c222B TEX-S2\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.896em; margin-left: -0.388em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" size=\"s\" style=\"margin-left: 0.647em;\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-spacer style=\"margin-top: 1.454em;\"></mjx-spacer><mjx-texatom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c28\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D465 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2B\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c29\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-texatom texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2F\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-texatom><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-texatom></mjx-script></mjx-msubsup><mjx-msubsup space=\"2\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-lop\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c222B TEX-S2\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.896em; margin-left: -0.388em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" size=\"s\" style=\"margin-left: 0.647em;\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-spacer style=\"margin-top: 1.513em;\"></mjx-spacer><mjx-texatom size=\"s\" texclass=\"ORD\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-texatom></mjx-script></mjx-msubsup><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"2\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D453 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c28\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D465 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2C\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" spac