    "q-82210": {
      "dom_id": "step-q82210",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Change the order of integration in the double integral \n${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14154008/assets/8287ba53b227ddc36aff486ea8d42a83203940ee265163320c19ad6cdb39089e.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the right boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is\n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{y}\n$$\n\nand the left boundary of the region is\n\n$$\nx=0.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type II region. The type II representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}\\},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14154008/assets/2c9a41f06d7edfbad9756923d9b70f1d0ffd730350d0b7d2d0e109c1bca9f80d.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-82210-a",
              "type": "math",
