    "q-82264": {
      "dom_id": "step-q82264",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Change the order of integration in the double integral \n${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}-1}^{1-{x}^{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14154008/assets/374acdaf337d1977f938fc66a19a8b933a4464f922c7e9fd45fd39a6cacf920e.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{2}-1\\le y\\le 1-{x}^{3}\\}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we need to split $D$ into two type II regions. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14154008/assets/cf06c4d0e0189b8b3e3c60af788c0aa082755db9b9fab17ed0562e79e11cabe9.png)\n\nNotice that the right boundary of the lower region, written in the form $x=x(y),$  is \n\n$\\,$ $x=\\sqrt{y+1}.$\n\nAlso, the right boundary of the upper region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$\\,$ $x=\\sqrt[3]{1-y}.$\n\nSo, we can write $D$ as a union of\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le y\\le 0,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y+1}\\}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt[3]{1-y}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}-1}^{1-{x}^{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{y+1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{1-y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-82264-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{1-y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{y+1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y",
