    "q-38467": {
      "dom_id": "step-q38467",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Change the order of integration and evaluate the following double integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{1}\\frac{3{x}^{5}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{6}+{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14154008/assets/a85f82756c621bf88b95451f54343be863345278f361fd0f0dd82f5d01c0cb5b.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{3}\\le y\\le 1\\}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the left boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is\n\n$$\nx=0,\n$$\n\nand the right boundary is\n\n$$\ny={x}^{3}\\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt[3]{y}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type II region. Its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt[3]{y}\\},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14154008/assets/8243a8c60e4b8b4846d330a00a090d6f93f94f17323c1d0a88d486ba77745451.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{3}}^{1}\\frac{3{x}^{5}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{6}+{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{y}}\\frac{3{x}^{5}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{6}+{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{y}}\\frac{3{x}^{5}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{6}+{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3{[\\frac{2}{6}\\sqrt{{x}^{6}+{y}^{2}}]}_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{y}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\sqrt{2{y}^{2}}-\\sqrt{{y}^{2}})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y(\\sqrt{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\sqrt{2}-1)}{2}[{y}^{2}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-38467-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\sqrt{2}-1",
              "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"166\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-msqrt><mjx-sqrt><mjx-surd><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c221A\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-surd><mjx-box style=\"padding-top: 0.174em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-box></mjx-sqrt></mjx-msqrt><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2212\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-38467-b",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\sqrt{2}+1",
              "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"167\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-msqrt><mjx-sqrt><mjx-surd><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c221A\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-surd><mjx-box style=\"padding-top: 0.174em;\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-box></mjx-sqrt></mjx-msqrt><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2B\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>"
